---@class aws.batch.EksEmptyDir
---@field medium? aws.batch.String The medium to store the volume. The default value is an empty string, which uses the storage of the node.
---@field sizeLimit? aws.batch.Quantity The maximum size of the volume. By default, there's no maximum size defined.

---Specifies the configuration of a Kubernetes hostPath volume. A hostPath volume mounts an existing file or directory from the host node's filesystem into your pod. For more information, see hostPath in the Kubernetes documentation.
---@class aws.batch.EksHostPath
---@field path? aws.batch.String The path of the file or directory on the host to mount into containers on the pod.

