---An object that represents an Batch job definition.
---@class aws.batch.JobDefinition
---@field jobDefinitionName aws.batch.String The name of the job definition.
---@field jobDefinitionArn aws.batch.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) for the job definition.
---@field revision aws.batch.Integer The revision of the job definition.
---@field status? aws.batch.String The status of the job definition.
---@field type aws.batch.String The type of job definition. It's either container or multinode. If the job is run on Fargate resources, then multinode isn't supported. For more information about multi-node parallel jobs, see Creating a multi-node parallel job definition in the Batch User Guide.
---@field schedulingPriority? aws.batch.Integer The scheduling priority of the job definition. This only affects jobs in job queues with a fair-share policy. Jobs with a higher scheduling priority are scheduled before jobs with a lower scheduling priority.
---@field parameters? aws.batch.ParametersMap Default parameters or parameter substitution placeholders that are set in the job definition. Parameters are specified as a key-value pair mapping. Parameters in a SubmitJob request override any corresponding parameter defaults from the job definition. For more information about specifying parameters, see Job definition parameters in the Batch User Guide.
---@field retryStrategy? aws.batch.RetryStrategy The retry strategy to use for failed jobs that are submitted with this job definition.
---@field containerProperties? aws.batch.ContainerProperties An object with properties specific to Amazon ECS-based jobs. When containerProperties is used in the job definition, it can't be used in addition to eksProperties, ecsProperties, or nodeProperties.
---@field timeout? aws.batch.JobTimeout The timeout time for jobs that are submitted with this job definition. After the amount of time you specify passes, Batch terminates your jobs if they aren't finished.
---@field nodeProperties? aws.batch.NodeProperties An object with properties that are specific to multi-node parallel jobs. When nodeProperties is used in the job definition, it can't be used in addition to containerProperties, ecsProperties, or eksProperties.
---@field tags? aws.batch.TagrisTagsMap The tags that are applied to the job definition.
---@field propagateTags? aws.batch.Boolean Specifies whether to propagate the tags from the job or job definition to the corresponding Amazon ECS task. If no value is specified, the tags aren't propagated. Tags can only be propagated to the tasks when the tasks are created. For tags with the same name, job tags are given priority over job definitions tags. If the total number of combined tags from the job and job definition is over 50, the...
---@field platformCapabilities? aws.batch.PlatformCapabilityList The platform capabilities required by the job definition. If no value is specified, it defaults to EC2. Jobs run on Fargate resources specify FARGATE. Jobs run on Amazon ECS Managed Instances specify MANAGED_INSTANCES.
---@field ecsProperties? aws.batch.EcsProperties An object that contains the properties for the Amazon ECS resources of a job.When ecsProperties is used in the job definition, it can't be used in addition to containerProperties, eksProperties, or nodeProperties.
---@field eksProperties? aws.batch.EksProperties An object with properties that are specific to Amazon EKS-based jobs. When eksProperties is used in the job definition, it can't be used in addition to containerProperties, ecsProperties, or nodeProperties.
---@field containerOrchestrationType? aws.batch.OrchestrationType The orchestration type of the compute environment. The valid values are ECS (default) or EKS.
---@field consumableResourceProperties? aws.batch.ConsumableResourceProperties Contains a list of consumable resources required by the job.

---@alias aws.batch.JobDefinitionList aws.batch.JobDefinition[]

---@alias aws.batch.JobDefinitionType "container"|"multinode"

