---@field createdAt? aws.batch.Long The Unix timestamp (in milliseconds) for when the job was created. For non-array jobs and parent array jobs, this is when the job entered the SUBMITTED state (at the time SubmitJob was called). For array child jobs, this is when the child job was spawned by its parent and entered the PENDING state.
---@field scheduledAt? aws.batch.Long The Unix timestamp (in milliseconds) for when the job was scheduled for execution. For more information on job statues, see Service job status in the Batch User Guide.
---@field shareIdentifier? aws.batch.String The share identifier for the fairshare scheduling queue that this job is associated with.
---@field status? aws.batch.JobStatus The current status for the job.
---@field statusReason? aws.batch.String A short, human-readable string to provide more details for the current status of the job.
---@field startedAt? aws.batch.Long The Unix timestamp for when the job was started. More specifically, it's when the job transitioned from the STARTING state to the RUNNING state.
---@field stoppedAt? aws.batch.Long The Unix timestamp for when the job was stopped. More specifically, it's when the job transitioned from the RUNNING state to a terminal state, such as SUCCEEDED or FAILED.
---@field container? aws.batch.ContainerSummary An object that represents the details of the container that's associated with the job.
---@field arrayProperties? aws.batch.ArrayPropertiesSummary The array properties of the job, if it's an array job.
---@field nodeProperties? aws.batch.NodePropertiesSummary The node properties for a single node in a job summary list.
---@field jobDefinition? aws.batch.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the job definition.
---@field isCancelled? aws.batch.Boolean Indicates whether a cancellation request has been accepted for the job. This field is only present when the value is true.
---@field isTerminated? aws.batch.Boolean Indicates whether a termination request has been accepted for the job. This field is only present when the value is true.

---@alias aws.batch.JobSummaryList aws.batch.JobSummary[]

